<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Pteria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 547 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Pteria was fought around 547 BCE in Cappadocia, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizilirmak">Halys</a> river, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus of Lydia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> the battle was indecisive and Croesus withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a> for the winter, but Cyrus followed him, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydians">Lydians</a> outside the city and took Sardis after a short siege. The independent kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> ended with this campaign.</p></div>
